### NestJS Mongoose CRUD API - HTTP Test Requests
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Root Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: text/plain

### ===============================
### USERS CRUD (Mapped to MongoDB Atlas 'users' collection)
### ===============================

### 2. Create User 1 (POST /users)
# @name createUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Saurabh Bhandari",
  "email": "saurabh@example.com",
  "role": "admin",
  "age": 25,
  "isActive": true
}

### 3. Create User 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "role": "user",
  "age": 28,
  "isActive": true
}

### 4. Get All Users (GET /users)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Accept: application/json

### 5. Get User by ID (GET /users/:id)
# Replace with the _id returned from createUser above
@userId = 658d4a22f98c657b2cea8f33
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Update User (PATCH /users/:id)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "age": 26,
  "isActive": false
}

### 7. Delete User (DELETE /users/:id)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### ===============================
### PRODUCTS CRUD
### ===============================

### 8. Create a Product (POST /products)
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ergonomic Mechanical Keyboard",
  "description": "Wireless mechanical keyboard with RGB backlighting and hot-swappable switches",
  "price": 129.99,
  "category": "Electronics",
  "inStock": true,
  "tags": ["peripherals", "keyboard", "wireless"]
}

### 3. Create a Second Product
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ultra-Wide Gaming Monitor 34-inch",
  "description": "144Hz curved gaming display with HDR400",
  "price": 499.50,
  "category": "Electronics",
  "inStock": true,
  "tags": ["monitor", "gaming", "ultrawide"]
}

### 4. Create a Third Product (Different Category)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ergonomic Desk Chair",
  "description": "Adjustable lumbar support breathable mesh chair",
  "price": 249.00,
  "category": "Furniture",
  "inStock": true,
  "tags": ["furniture", "ergonomic", "office"]
}

### 5. Get All Products (GET /products)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products
Accept: application/json

### 6. Filter & Paginate Products
# Filter by category and price range with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?category=Electronics&minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&page=1&limit=5
Accept: application/json

### 7. Search Products by Text Index
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?search=Mechanical
Accept: application/json

### 8. Get Product by ID (GET /products/:id)
# Replace with an actual ObjectID returned from POST /products
@productId = 507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Partially Update Product (PATCH /products/:id)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 109.99,
  "inStock": false
}

### 10. Delete Product (DELETE /products/:id)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Accept: application/json

### 11. Test Validation: Invalid Payload (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "A",
  "price": -10,
  "unknownField": "not allowed"
}

### 12. Test Validation: Invalid MongoDB ID format (Should return 400 Bad Request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/not-a-valid-id
Accept: application/json

